# ---------------------------------------------------------------- RouteWatch
#
# Two categories are deliberately kept out of the repository.
#
# 1. CACHED API CONTENT
#    AeroDataBox Terms of Use, Article 5.5, caps cached Contents at seven days,
#    and 5.2(g) forbids building a permanent database out of them. A file that is
#    committed lives in git history forever, which is the opposite of a cache.
#    RouteWatch reads these CSVs on every run and keeps only its own computed
#    results, so nothing of value is lost by not committing them.
#
# 2. THE IMMERSION VARIANT
#    docs/community-immersion.json carries flight numbers, departure times and
#    airline per route. Those are Contents, not a Derived Work. Anything under
#    docs/ is served publicly by GitHub Pages, so committing it would publish it.
#    It stays ignored until AeroDataBox confirms in writing that the Plan Terms
#    permit showing those fields to end users (Articles 5.6 and 5.3).
#
#    Remove those two lines once that permission is on paper.

# Cached API responses, seven-day retention
data/manual/*.csv

# Flight-level variant: not public until permission is in writing
docs/community-immersion.json
data/community-immersion.json

# Local scanner output: describes one person's machine, not the project
data/sim-scan.json
data/sim-scan.md
config/collection.scan.json

# Reports regenerated on every run
data/retention-check.md
data/variant-comparison.md

# Local noise
node_modules/
.DS_Store
.env
*.log
